.terraform/
.terraform.tfstate.lock.info
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfvars
!terraform.tfvars.example
crash.log
override.tf
override.tf.json
*_override.tf
*_override.tf.json
# `secrets/` (the whole directory) until 2026-09-06. That was correct about
# plaintext and wrong about everything else: git does not descend into an
# ignored directory, so `.sops.yaml`'s own `path_regex: infra/secrets/.*`
# creation rule could never have produced a committable file, and neither
# could `load-secrets.sh --encrypt`. Encrypted material is the point of the
# directory; ignoring it wholesale ignored the ciphertext too.
# The directory now governs itself, deny-by-default, in infra/secrets/.gitignore.
secrets/*
!secrets/.gitignore
